```sql
{% macro cents_to_dollars(column_name, scale=2) %}
  {{ function('cents_to_dollars') }}({{ column_name }}, {{scale}})
{% endmacro %}
```

### Debugging Macros
If you need to debug a macro, you can insert the `debug()` function inside the macro definition. When dbt compiles the project, it will drop you into an interactive debugger at that line [4].

File: `my_macro.sql`
